# Patch files must always use LF line endings - CRLF corrupts them and
# breaks `patch` (typically fails right at EOF with "malformed patch" or
# "unexpectedly ends in middle of line"). This overrides any
# core.autocrlf=true setting (the Git for Windows default) for these
# specific files, regardless of which platform clones/checks out the repo.
*.patch text eol=lf
